# granite-shallows - machine-readable palette
#
# Format: one role=hex per line, grouped into [sections] that carry no meaning
# to a parser. Read it by line shape rather than by looking for an "=", since
# comments contain those too:
#
#   grep -E '^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*=#[0-9A-Fa-f]{6}$' granite-shallows.colors
#
# Sampled from an alpine lake shore: deep blue water and sky, turquoise
# shallows, granite boulders, snow on the far range.
#
# ONE color, at hue 242. The turquoise shallows are a real presence in the
# image - 15.3% by chroma-weighted share, at hue 202 - but they fail two gates
# at once. They are 40 degrees from the main axis where 45 is needed to count
# as a separate color rather than the same blue lighter, and 19 degrees from
# catppuccin teal where an optional secondary needs 20. Sky, deep water and
# shallows here really are one blue-cyan family.
#
# 16.9% of the image is effectively grey, chroma under 0.02 - the boulders,
# which are the subject but contribute no hue. That is the highest grey share
# of any wallpaper in this set.
#
# The band spans about 25 degrees centered on 242, inside the widest STATUS gap
# on the wheel (catppuccin teal 182.7 to mauve 304.8). Closest approach to a
# status hue is 49 degrees. Note that this lane is not empty of catppuccin's
# SYNTAX colors, which nvim renders: sapphire sits at 228.7 and blue at 259.9.
# accent_light lands dE 0.011 from sapphire, which is a genuine near-match.
# That is advisory rather than disqualifying - see the skill - and the role
# that now matters most, accent_bright, is dE 0.049 from its nearest catppuccin
# color, the largest separation of any palette here.
#
# Same 21 roles and the same lightness and chroma per role as the other
# palettes. Only hue moved, plus accent's lightness, which build raises to hold
# 4.5:1 because WCAG luminance is hue-dependent.
#
# Provenance, measured rather than asserted (palette.py check --image):
# 15 of 21 roles are within dE 0.03 of a color the photograph contains. The
# dark and mid roles are genuine samples - bg at dE 0.002, accent at 0.008. The
# TOP OF THE TEXT RAMP IS NOT: the image never exceeds lightness 0.892 and
# text_bright needs 0.967, so text_bright, text, cursor and accent_bright are
# extrapolated up the hue axis. This wallpaper has no lit snow close enough to
# sample, unlike alpine-haze's.
#
# Semantic colors stay catppuccin mocha. Claude Code's shimmers are computed
# from the roles below by palettes/recompute_shimmers.py, not stored here.
# Hex case is not significant here but it is in the configs; match
# case-insensitively when substituting.

[background]
bg=#12202E
bg_surface=#192D3F
bg_raised=#353F47
bg_selection=#325371

[text]
text_bright=#EEF5F9
text=#D1E4F1
text_secondary=#A7B3BD
text_muted=#8CA4C0
text_dim=#6890AE
text_hint=#8B97A1

[chrome]
border=#59656E
cursor=#9CD7F6
accent=#518BBF
accent_bright=#B4D8F2
accent_light=#7FC7ED
accent_soft=#8EADD0
accent_vivid=#4FB5E8

[reserve]
# reserve_1 is no longer spare: it paints nvim's folder names and folder
# icon, one step darker than the files on accent_bright. reserve_2..4
# still render nothing and are named by position rather than by job.
# Promote one into a real role rather than adding a new hex.
reserve_1=#63B9DD
reserve_2=#5DA7DB
reserve_3=#5798D5
reserve_4=#355674
